    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task was to make `POST /api/owners` (read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`) return `selfLink` = `/api/owners/` followed by the new owner id.\n\nI followed the codebase's existing pattern for derived, read-only owner fields (like `displayName`, `salutation`, `membershipNumber`), where a getter lives on the domain entity and MapStruct maps it into the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `selfLink` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema. The code generator produces the corresponding `OwnerDto` field/getter at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added `getSelfLink()`, which derives the value from the owner's own id (`\"/api/owners/\" + id`), returning `null` until an id is assigned. This keeps the logic in the entity alongside the other id/derived accessors, with a single responsibility, and MapStruct maps it automatically \u2014 no controller or mapper changes needed.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsSelfLink` test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
